"[HEADER] Installation Infos",
"kill",
"Requires PC port of the game. Can be downloaded via the 'Game' tab if you don't already have the game.\n\nWhen you click 'START SETUP' in the 'SETUP' tab, simpsonshitnrun.apworld will be installed and moved into the 'custom_worlds' folder inside the Archipelago Launcher directory. SHAR Mod Launcher into the 'Documents' directory.\nThe required AP Mod file "SHARAP.lmlm" will be installed inside Documents\\My Games\\Lucas' Simpsons Hit & Run Mod Launcher\\Mods\\SHARAP.lmlm.\nThe Archipelago Randomizer folder (containing the app used for connecting to the AP servers) will be installed inside the game's folder.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] apworld / yaml Infos",
"kill",
"SHAR is not a core Archipelago game, it needs a custom world file. When 'simpsonshitnrun.apworld' is downloaded in the Archipelago Folder (by clicking START SETUP), boot-up the Archipelago Launcher and go to 'Options Creator' to create your .yaml file and then, when you're done, send it to the person who will host the AP Multiworld.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"Let's say you didn't have any launch option enabled.\nOnce everything is set up, launch 'SHARRandomizerFrontend.exe' inside the new Archipelago folder in your game's folder and launch the Archipelago Launcher.\nWith the newly installed simpsonshitnrun.apworld file, you should be able to find a new 'Simpsons Hit & Run Client' in the AP Launcher. Don't open it yet. The host of your Archipelago session will need to go to the Archipelago website and go to the room that you are going to use for your Archipelago session. There, you should be able to find a button that says 'Download Patch File' next to your name. Download it, and once you have it, you can move on to the next step.\n\nYou can now open the 'Simpsons Hit & Run Client' and it will ask you to select the path to certain executables. When it is asking you to 'Select a .apshar patch' you will need to select the patch file that you just downloaded from the website. Then, it should open the game.\n\nNow go back to 'SHARRandomizerFrontend.exe'.\n\nIn the 'Server' field, enter archipelago.gg.\n\nIn 'Port' enter the room’s 5-digit port number. You can find this number on the website after creating a new room.\n\nIn 'Slot', enter the name assigned to your YAML file.\n\nThe 'Password' field is optional. If the host did not set one, leave it blank.\n\nFinally, click 'Connect' and then, you can start a new run!\n\nNow, go back to the game and you should be able to start a game while connected to the AP server! :)",
"kill",
"[HEADER] PopTracker Infos",
"kill",
"Some games have a PopTracker integration for Archipelago which allows you to track all possible Locations, Items, Upgrades, Zones, Hints and more depending on the game.\n\nFor the setup there are 3 different cases:\n\n\t• If the selected directory does not contain a PopTracker folder (or any similarly named folder), a new 'poptracker' folder will be created and the pack will be downloaded to poptracker\\packs.\n\n\t• If the selected directory already contains a folder with 'PopTracker' in its name, the installer will look for a poptracker.exe file. If one is found, the pack will be downloaded to its packs folder. If no poptracker.exe is found, the folder will be renamed to 'poptracker' and any missing files or folders will be created.\n\n\t• If the selected directory is already a PopTracker folder (for example: C:\\Users\\magni\\Documents\\poptracker), its contents will be validated. If everything is present, the pack will simply be downloaded to poptracker\\packs. Otherwise, the folder will be repaired before the pack is installed.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Troubleshoot",
"kill",
"If you launch the Mod Launcher for the first time with the launch option related to it and it says that some framework or mods are required, it shouldn't do anything and I would assume it is just a false error (seems like it).\n\nIf you game doesn't launch with the AP Mod loaded when using the Client, open the Mod Launcher and make sure the 'Archipelago' mod is enabled.\n\nFeel free to report anything (or simply join the discord) here!",
